# KNOWN GAP — Core #8, BOTH BACKENDS: `Guard.get()` passed as a TEMP into a
# collection-mutator consuming position double-frees.
#
#   C backend    : prints `1`, then `free(): double free detected in tcache 2`,
#                  SIGABRT (exit 134)
#   LLVM backend : identical
#
# INTENDED: `1`, exit 0. `g.get()` yields a view INTO the mutex-owned payload;
# a consuming position must CLONE it, never hand the collection a shallow alias
# that both the dict and the mutex will free.
#
# SCOPE — one cell of the DESTINATION axis, and the discriminator is TEMP vs
# NAMED LOCAL, not the destination:
#   d.put("k", g.get())                  <-- BROKEN (this fixture)
#   String s = g.get(); d.put("k", s)    <-- exit 0, correct
# The same temp-vs-named-local split governs the sibling `push` cell, which
# fails EARLIER (a check-time consume-site panic rather than a runtime abort):
#   sink.push(g.get())  -> PANIC, src/ir/lowering/mod.rs:2143,
#                          "CollectionMutator(Vector__GorgetString__push,
#                           arg #1) -- borrowed source consumed"
#
# Sibling cells that are CORRECT at HEAD (fixed by 1d892511, 2026-07-28) and so
# are NOT part of this gap: `String s = g.get()`, `return g.get()`,
# `Holder(g.get())`. Those three shipped with no coverage at all; live fixtures
# for them are owed separately.
#
# WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS AT ALL: the cell was twice mis-recorded from
# inference rather than measurement -- first as broken (inherited from a scout
# that grouped ctor and put into one row), then as green (that row was split
# and the ctor measurement carried across). Measured 2026-08-05 by direct
# binary invocation. Reproduces with the read-back removed, so it is the put,
# not the print.
#
# HEAP-FORCED VALUE (never a literal -- a rodata String has cap=0, so
# gorget_string_free short-circuits and the bug reads as absent).
#
# Graduate out of known_gaps/ (un-ignore + move) the round this is fixed.

String heaped():
    return "hello " + "world" + "-forced"

void main():
    Mutex[String] m = Mutex[String](heaped())
    Guard[String] g = m.lock()
    Dict[String, String] d = {}
    d.put("k", g.get())
    print(d.len())
